283 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 284 0 R/Alt(A column of eight boxes joined by downward arrows, with a curved arrow from the last back to the first labeled next loop. The boxes read: 1, play the drive in force at the present level; 2, estimate the response matrix and refer it to full level; 3, judge it against the abort lines and for a growing error; 4, the law, with the target, the measured response and the frequency response in and the next drive out, drawn with an orange dashed outline; 5, check the drive for size, numbers, Hermitian form and zero out of band, repair a small negative eigenvalue and refuse a large one; 6, cap each drive's change at plus 3.5 dB and minus 6 dB a loop; 7, hold each drive's ceiling and limit the limit channels; 8, keep it as the drive in force. The other seven boxes have blue solid outlines. A legend says blue solid is the core, the same for every law, and orange dashed is the control law.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[45]/Pg 2505 0 R>>
endobj
