669 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 670 0 R/Alt(Three panels. The left and middle panels plot error against the target in decibels from 20 to 600 Hz on a log axis, for gauge 1 and gauge 2. An orange dashed line, the open loop, swings by up to about 5 dB at gauge 1 and 7 dB at gauge 2 around four resonances near 90, 160, 260 and 410 Hz. A green dotted line, the closed loop after 5 loops, is near zero except for narrow dips at the resonances. A blue solid line, after 30 loops, lies on zero at gauge 1 and at gauge 2 except for two narrow peaks of about 5 and 3 dB near 90 and 160 Hz. The right panel plots RMS error over the band against loop number from 0 to 30: the open loop is flat at about 1.5 dB for both gauges, drawn as orange dotted and dash-dot lines; gauge 1 closed loop, blue with filled circles, falls to near zero by loop 20; gauge 2 closed loop, green dashed with open squares, falls to about 0.4 dB by loop 10 and stays there.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[25]/Pg 2511 0 R>>
endobj
