1130 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 1131 0 R/Alt(Two panels. Left: drive power, the trace of the drive matrix, against the phase of the cross term from minus 180 to 180 degrees. A black dotted flat line at about 0.96 is coherence 0. A green dashed curve, coherence 0.5, runs from about 0.4 at plus and minus 180 degrees to about 1.5 at 0. A blue solid curve, coherence 1, runs from about 0.17 at plus and minus 180 degrees to about 1.74 at 0. Right: relative drive power on a log scale against the error in the autospectra from 0 to 2, with open blue circles joined by a line. Five grid points from 10 to the minus 6 to 0.01 sit together at zero error and the highest drive, labeled autospectra met with the least drive that meets them; the first of them, at 10 to the minus 6, is marked with a large orange star as picked by the rule with the 3 dB largest shortfall; a point at 0.1 sits at error 0.63; the point at 1, marked with an open black diamond as the knee alone, sits at error 0.72 and about one fortieth of the highest drive; points from 10 up sit at error 2 with no drive.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[105]/Pg 2518 0 R>>
endobj
