1204 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 1205 0 R/Alt(Two panels sharing a log frequency axis from 30 to 500 Hz. Top: gauge response in decibels relative to the target. The target is a black line at 0 dB from 40 to 500 Hz. The response line by line, a blue dashed line, swings by up to about plus 6 and minus 14 dB around resonances near 120 and 310 Hz and stays within about 1 dB elsewhere. Open black circles mark the target's one-sixth-octave band averages at 0 dB, and orange triangles the response's band averages, which sit on the circles in every band except one near 94 Hz, at minus 1.9 dB, labeled the band where the drive costs most. Bottom: drive in decibels on an arbitrary reference. A green solid step line, the band-average drive, is flat within each band and follows an orange dotted line, the drive that would match every line, falling from about 43 dB at 40 Hz to about minus 20 dB near 310 Hz, without its narrow peak near 95 Hz or its narrow dips near 120 and 330 Hz.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[0]/Pg 2521 0 R>>
endobj
